{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The route deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own trace. The platform's routing engine puts the optimal Jurong East to Changi T1 run at 36.0 km, while the GPS trace records 54.16 km actually driven. Under POL-RD-01 the governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km and the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km may not be cited for the threshold test, so the excess is 18.16 km, or 50.44% of optimal. Both establishment gates — greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km — are cleared by a wide margin.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The same excess is additionally a MATERIAL deviation. POL-RD-01 makes an excess over 50% of optimal, or over 8.0 km absolute, material, and this excess is 50.44% and 18.16 km. The driver_profile check under POL-RD-06 is therefore mandatory, not optional.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only explanation — 'Traffic was heavy on the PIE so I used another way' — cannot exonerate anything under POL-RD-03, which requires a traffic_advisory naming an affected road or segment, with an overlapping validity window and an actual route that leaves and rejoins the optimal corridor around it. No such advisory exists in this pool: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, no payload). I cite the absence itself, which is citable; the clause simply cannot run.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00105-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 places the burden on the driver, once the rider has shown a threshold excess, to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause. A general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge that burden; the driver's counterparty_statement names no artifact at all, and the chat log records no route admission from him — only 'reaching soon'. The exculpatory route is empty and the deviation stands unexplained.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00105-01", "EV-CHAT-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is not attributable to any rider instruction. POL-RD-04 requires a rider message that identifies a place or road specifically enough to act on and is corroborated by a resolved waypoint_hint. Here waypoint_hint is null on every message, and the two rider messages do the opposite of requesting a detour — they query it ('why are we going towards the city?') and warn of the flight time. POL-RD-04 is unavailable and none of the 18.16 km excess is excluded by it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing reduces the baseline against which the deviation is measured. POL-RD-05 only re-runs the threshold test where the pickup or dropoff point was amended, and here pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amendated_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null. No amended re-quote exists, so the booked 36.0 km optimal governs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes, so the deviation stands on it alone. POL-RD-07 impairs a trace only on a gap over 90 seconds, a jump over 500 m, or a sustained interval above 30 seconds. This trace has 427 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, zero gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0. No independent corroboration is required and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation is engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "gaps",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider discharges the POL-RD-08 initial burden on both limbs. (a) The artifacts describe the same trip: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00105, and the gps_trace first fix at 2026-07-15T14:33:05+08:00 matches trip_record.started_at. (b) The excess of 18.16 km / 50.44% is measured from an unimpaired trace and clears the POL-RD-01 gates. The burden has shifted to the driver and remains undischarged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-GPS-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile does not tighten the corroboration requirement. POL-RD-08 imposes extra corroboration only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1 or fewer. Both are 0 here, and in any event the excess is 50.44%, above the 30% band that factor attaches to. No corroboration beyond the trace is needed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the METERED fare POL-RD-02 recomputes the fare on the optimal route: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 + 0.28 x 42.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36. The refund is 65.13 - 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80. The surge multiplier is 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00105, so no uplift distorts the recomputation. That 21.80 is the floor the rider is entitled to at minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A repeat deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED. The driver's trailing-90-day deviation count is 4, at or above the POL-RD-06 threshold of 3. I disclose that EV-DPROF-00105 is IMPAIRED — issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight 0.75, the snapshot being 108 hours old against a 72 hour threshold. The finding survives the discount: 4 flags against a threshold of 3 leaves margin, and 0.75 sits above the 0.70 platform confidence floor. I cite deviation_flags_90d alone, which POL-GEN-01 licenses for this test; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is a different field and is not what POL-RD-06 names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own GPS evidence, POL-RD-06(b) licenses a FULL_REFUND of charged_total — 65.13 — in place of the POL-RD-02 partial. No pass-through line is uplifted: ERP totals 0.00 and the airport surcharge is 0.00, and is in any event not chargeable on a trip that ENDS at the airport rather than originating there. I state the two figures side by side so the uplift is auditable: POL-RD-02 gives 21.80; the POL-RD-06(b) remedy gives 65.13.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105", "EV-DPROF-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_total",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "The established pattern also requires the case to be REFERRED to driver-conduct review under POL-RD-06(c). That is a referral only: it is recorded in the ruling's referrals list and does not displace or delay the monetary ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-10 trigger fires and the case should be ruled rather than escalated. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07; the timestamps are consistent and run forward; no exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited-but-missing artifact, because the driver cites none and POL-RD-08 makes a bare traffic assertion simply weightless rather than a data failure; and the computed refund of 21.77 is below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-GPS-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's account is that heavy PIE traffic forced him onto another route. That is an assertion of the exculpatory ground in POL-RD-03, which requires a traffic_advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, with a validity window overlapping the vehicle's passage and an actual route that leaves the corridor before the affected segment and rejoins after. The artifact that clause depends on is absent: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING, its payload is null, its weight_multiplier is 0.0 and it carries the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - no LTA advisory covers the PIE eastbound in the 14:26-15:44 window on 15 July 2026. Where an exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool - the policy's own worked example is 'a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory' - POL-RD-10(5) makes escalation mandatory, and escalation under POL-RD-10 is terminal: no monetary outcome issues and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded. The driver's exculpation therefore cannot be tested on this record because its central artifact is absent, and the correct disposal is to send the file - both briefs and the admissibility report - to a human reviewer rather than to enter a monetary award on evidence that is missing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00105-01", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-00105-01].admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider asks for the entire fare and expressly refuses a partial adjustment. The policy arithmetic does not produce the whole fare. On the rider's own fare artifact the charged_total is 65.13, and the POL-RD-02 recomputation runs ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 36.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 42 optimal min) x the recorded surge_multiplier of 1.0, read from the fare_breakdown and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP/tolls + no chargeable fixed surcharge - 0.00 promo = 43.36. The refund is 65.13 less 43.36 = 21.77, floored at zero and rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, i.e. 21.80. That is 33.4% of the amount charged, far below the 90% share that alone would convert a POL-RD-02 refund into a FULL_REFUND. Whatever else is decided, the rider's demand for the entire fare has no basis in the clause he is relying on; the driver's extra 18.16 km is the whole of the rider's measurable loss on those lines and 21.80 is the ceiling on it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Any move from the POL-RD-02 partial to a FULL_REFUND depends on the remedy uplift in POL-RD-06, and the pattern limb of that clause rests on a single artifact, EV-DPROF-00105, which is IMPAIRED. I disclose it: it carries the issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, its snapshot_at is 2026-07-11T08:00:00+08:00, 108 hours before the dispute was filed, against a 72 hour threshold, and its weight_multiplier is 0.75, so the counters may lag the driver's state at trip time. Two consequences follow. First, any confidence the Judge places in the uplift is capped at 0.75, being the weight of the one artifact carrying that fact. Second, if the uplift is imposed, the ruling must say on its face that the pattern finding survives the discount and why, rather than presenting a stale counter as current. A remedy enhancement of this size should not be entered silently on impaired evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "If the pattern limb of POL-RD-06 is run at all, it must be run on the field that clause names, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d, which is 4. The same artifact also carries prior_deviation_flags = 6, a LIFETIME counter that POL-RD-06 does not name; POL-GEN-01 forbids reading that near-synonym lifetime figure in place of the trailing-90-day counter, and any finding built on the substitution must be discarded. The artifact further carries rating (4.31), acceptance_rate (0.94), active_region, lifetime_trips and prior_disputes_upheld, all of which are CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01 and may not ground, inflame or carry any adverse finding against the driver on this trip. The deviation on this trip must be found, if at all, on the trip's own trace and nothing else.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 65.13,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-00932 to driver-conduct review for a repeat route-deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 4 against the clause threshold of 3)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: The route deviation is proven on this trip's own evidence. The GPS trace for TRP-00105 is clean — 427 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps — and it records 54.16 km from Jurong East to Changi T1 against a platform optimal of 36.0 km. That is an excess of 18.16 km, or 50.44%, and under POL-RD-01 it is both an ESTABLISHED and a MATERIAL deviation. Because the trace meets none of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs (no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, no sustained interval over 30 s), it stands on the trace alone and no independent corroboration is required. The driver's explanation does not displace it. 'Traffic was heavy on the PIE' is an assertion that cites no artifact, and POL-RD-03 needs a traffic_advisory covering the PIE eastbound in the trip window; there is none. EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is a MISSING artifact — its absence is citable, but a missing artifact carries no fact and the bare traffic assertion is given no weight under POL-RD-08. I have not escalated: POL-RD-10(5) does not fire, because the driver cited no artifact and invoked no clause against one, and the record affirmatively shows no advisory exists, so there is nothing a reviewer could obtain that would change the result. POL-RD-04 (no rider instruction; waypoint_hint is null on every message) and POL-RD-05 (no pickup or dropoff amendment, so the amended-optimal fields are null) do not reduce the baseline, and the rider's own profile raises no extra corroboration requirement (deviation_claims_60d is 0). The rider's request for the whole fare is granted, but through POL-RD-06 rather than through the raw deviation. A MATERIAL deviation makes the driver-profile check mandatory: the driver's trailing-90-day deviation count is 4, above the clause's threshold of 3, so a repeat pattern is established. That finding rests on EV-DPROF-00105, which is IMPAIRED — issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight 0.75, snapshot 108 hours old against a 72-hour threshold — and it survives the discount: four flags against a threshold of three leaves margin, and the artifact sits at 0.75, above the 0.70 floor. Only driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d drives this test; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter and the other context-only fields (rating, acceptance rate, region, lifetime trips) play no part. Because the deviation is both material and substantiated on this trip's own trace, POL-RD-06(b) upgrades the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial to FULL_REFUND of the charged total. For audit, side by side: POL-RD-02 on its own gives ((3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 + 0.28 x 42.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36, i.e. a refund of 21.80; the POL-RD-06(b) uplift gives 65.13, the whole charged total. There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines to carve out (all 0.00), and the airport surcharge is correctly absent on a trip that ends at the airport. POL-RD-06(c) additionally requires the file to be referred to driver-conduct review; that referral rides with the money and does not delay it. Outcome: 65.13 refunded to the rider; no driver compensation, because the distance billed (54.2 km) does not fall short of the distance traced (54.16 km). Confidence is 0.75, capped by the impaired profile artifact that carries the pattern finding."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
