    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To both parties — this is decided on the platform's own telemetry.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. The routing engine put the optimal Jurong East–Changi T1 run at 36.0 km. The GPS trace, which POL-RD-01 makes the governing measurement (not the rounded trip-record copy), records 54.16 km. The excess is 18.16 km, or 50.44% of optimal. That clears both establishment gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km) and the MATERIAL gate (over 50% and over 8.0 km). The trace is unimpaired — 427 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps — so no POL-RD-07 consequence and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION CANNOT BE WEIGHED. 'Traffic was heavy on the PIE' is a general traffic assertion. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic advisory naming a road the optimal route uses, with an overlapping validity window, and none exists: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is missing from the pool. Under POL-RD-08 a general traffic assertion that cites no advisory carries no weight. It is also not an escalation: the driver points to no artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) — which governs a clause invoked against a cited-but-missing artifact — does not fire, and the driver's escalation request is rejected. POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 change nothing either: no rider message requested the detour (every waypoint_hint is null, and the rider's messages query the route and flag the flight time), and there is no pickup or dropoff amendment.\n\nTHE MONEY. On the METERED fare, POL-RD-02 gives ((3.80 + 0.75 × 36.0 + 0.28 × 42.0) × the 1.0 surge read from the fare breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36, so the refund is 65.13 − 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80. The driver is right that 21.80 is the ceiling of POL-RD-02 — but not of the case. The driver's profile shows 4 deviation flags in the trailing 90 days, so POL-RD-06 establishes a repeat pattern, and because this trip's deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on its own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) raises the remedy from the partial to FULL_REFUND of charged_total. Side by side, for audit: POL-RD-02 = 21.80; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted = 65.13. No pass-through line is uplifted — ERP and tolls are 0.00, and no airport surcharge is chargeable on a trip that ENDS at the airport rather than originating there.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The pattern finding rests on EV-DPROF-00105, which is impaired: issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight 0.75, its snapshot 108 hours old against a 72-hour threshold. The finding survives the discount — 4 flags against a threshold of 3 leaves margin — but POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at that artifact's 0.75, which is above the 0.70 floor, so the case is ruled rather than escalated.\n\nREFERRAL. POL-RD-06(c) adds the driver-conduct referral recorded above; a referral never suppresses or delays the money.\n\nNOTE ON THE RIDER'S OWN CLAIMS. The rider's separate claims seeking the POL-RD-06(b) uplift and the POL-RD-06(c) referral were mechanically discarded for citing EV-DPROF-00105 without naming its STALE_SNAPSHOT code. The clause nonetheless operates on the surviving pattern claim, so the uplift and referral issue; the discarded claims are not themselves relied on."
  },
